. We rolled back all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and why it was promoted even though staging was unhealthy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55188, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XfdW5JnTPiCUg62vT2NydY", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_not_found", "safe_retry_with_key", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55188, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XfdW5JnTPiCUg62vT2NydY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59200, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n1. **What was wrong:** All three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1. The service was failing health checks, with 18% of requests returning errors.\n2. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2) for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It says what failed, what I rolled back, and that the service is healthy now. It also asks for two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 broke, and why it was released when its test version (v2.3.1-rc) had already been failing health checks in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01D9UNXW8b4Xhy6CYTEx57R2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Ph74Q2CCcP1g9USEXNf5qA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AWozZrZLBKLndEpzMkEWDV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NNspctP4qHqZKTMVFiiUct", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Eq3NVrBJtDJuJivZ7niZzh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XfdW5JnTPiCUg62vT2NydY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled back all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and why it was promoted even though staging was unhealthy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n1. **What was wrong:** All three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1. The service was failing health checks, with 18% of requests returning errors.\n2. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2) for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It says what failed, what I rolled back, and that the service is healthy now. It also asks for two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 broke, and why it was released when its test version (v2.3.1-rc) had already been failing health checks in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}